W-EH5 Comments:
Discharge of wastewater to land or water in accordance with sections 15(1)(a) and 15(1)(b) of the Resource Management Act 1991 as a result of:
• network overflows during periods of wet weather flow;
• network overflows resulting solely from blockages or network failure (pipe collapse or breakage or power or mechanical failure at pump stations or storage chambers);
• network exfiltration
for the existing Papakura District Wastewater Network.

Discharge of wastewater to land or water in accordance with sections 15(1)(a) and 15(1)(b) of the Resource Management Act 1991 as a result of:
• network overflows during periods of wet weather flow;
• network overflows resulting solely from blockages or network failure (pipe collapse or breakage or power or mechanical failure at pump stations or storage chambers);
• network exfiltration
for the existing and future Hingaia Peninsula Growth Area Wastewater Network.

Discharge of wastewater to land or water in accordance with sections 15(1)(a) and 15(1)(b) of the Resource Management Act 1991 as a result of:
• network overflows during periods of wet weather flow;
• network overflows resulting solely from blockages or network failure (pipe collapse or breakage or power or mechanical failure at pump stations or storage chambers);
• network exfiltration
for the existing and future Takanini Growth Area Wastewater Network.
